<launch>
  <!--
    object_mission.launch — "pick an object, then fly to it and land".

    The select-then-go mission on top of the FALCON stack. It is
    real_drone_object_approach.launch with two differences:

      1. GATED START. object_approach comes up DISABLED (start_enabled:=false), so
         no visual servo runs and nothing lands until an object is selected. (The
         platform still takes off and hovers in place — that is the follower's
         baseline; only the mission is gated.)
         The nav stack takes goal_x/goal_y, which default to a real coordinate, so
         A* DOES plan a route at startup and flies it on GO. Set them empty to
         restore the older behaviour where the planners idle until a click too.
         Note the GO gate is separate and independent: with start_go:=false not one
         velocity command reaches the drone whatever the planners are doing.

      2. A MISSION DIRECTOR. mission_director_node loads objects.json and, on
         selection (random pick, or a click in its object-list window), publishes the
         object's LABEL (-> YOLO re-prompt + object_approach gate, /object_approach/goal),
         a coordinate goal (-> planners, /waypoint_nav/goal), the object's own WORLD
         (x,y) (-> /object_approach/object_position), and enable=True (-> arms
         object_approach). That single act starts the mission.

    TWO POINTS. Before any object is picked the drone flies to a PRE-SELECTION TARGET
    (goal_x/goal_y, 0,-2) and simply HOLDS there in the air — object_approach is
    disabled, so nothing aims, sweeps, hands off /cmd_vel or lands. Picking an object
    arms the mission and sends the drone to a SEPARATE ROOM CENTRE (stage_x/stage_y,
    0,-3), which is where it looks for the object.

    THE STAGED APPROACH (stage_x / stage_y, on by default). The post-selection goal is
    NOT the object: it is the room centre. The catalogued object position comes from
    the room map and is only as good as that map — fly onto it and a small error can
    leave the object beside or behind the drone, out of frame, with nothing to servo
    onto. So on selection the mission:
      1. flies to the room centre;
      2. TURNS to look down the object's bearing and holds still there (AIM), because a
         camera resolves a bearing far better than a map resolves a position — this is
         the shot most likely to give the visual servo a real lock;
      3. if that look finds nothing, SWEEPS the room in place for it (aim_fail_to_scan),
         a slow rotate-with-stops turn — it never flies onto the object's own imprecise
         coordinate. (Set aim_fail_to_scan:=false to fall back to the older escalate:
         re-publish the goal at the object's (x,y) and fly the last leg.)
    Clear stage_x/stage_y to switch staging off and fly straight at the object, as before.

    Reaching the object ends the mission by LANDING; and if it is never found, the sweep
    gives up and lands too:
      * VISUAL reach (the success land): the detector confirms the object, object_approach
        servos onto it and lands when the depth range holds <= land_range_m.
      * GIVE-UP after the sweep: the room sweep turned scan_land_revolutions full turns
        (3) without a confirmation — the object is nowhere in the room, so land where we
        are. Arrival-land "by A* alone" is OFF here (land_at_goal:=false), so arriving at
        the room centre aims/sweeps and never lands by mere arrival.
    Either way the node stops /cmd_vel and requests 'finish' (stop -> land -> disarm via
    the demo manager).

    Run (in the FALCON container; the YOLO-World detector sidecar + bridge run on the
    host, see run_object_mission.sh / the README):

      roslaunch falcon_adapter object_mission.launch \
          map_name:=office selection_mode:=gui nav_mode:=fallback

    NOTE: start from a fresh roscore (run_falcon.sh's ephemeral container gives one) so a
    stale latched /waypoint_nav/goal from a previous run cannot pre-arm the planners.
  -->

  <!-- ── Shared / nav ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <arg name="map_name"        default="office" />
  <arg name="drone_ns"        default="" />
  <arg name="image_transport" default="frame_path" /><!-- frame_path (real drone) | topic (sim / bag) -->
  <!-- Localization source (world pose). Feeds the whole nav stack AND object_approach's
       arrival detection (so arrival-land works). Set to your pose topic, e.g.
       real_pose_topic:=/xtend/april_tag_pose for AprilTag localization. -->
  <arg name="real_pose_topic" default="/xtend/localization" />
  <arg name="real_pose_type"  default="pose_stamped" />     <!-- pose_stamped | pose -->
  <!-- ══ TWO DISTINCT POINTS: the room centre, and the pre-selection target ══════
       This mission waits at one fixed point BEFORE any object is picked, then works
       from a SEPARATE vantage point once one is. The two used to be the same
       coordinate; they are now independent, so the drone can hold at 0,-2 and look
       for objects from 0,-3.

       stage_x/stage_y — THE ROOM CENTRE (post-selection vantage point). On selecting
         an object the director republishes /waypoint_nav/goal HERE, NOT onto the
         object: the drone flies over, turns to look down the object's bearing (AIM),
         and if it does not see it, sweeps the room in place for it. It is also
         object_approach's arrival goal, so the two cannot drift apart.
         WHY not fly at the object itself: its catalogued position comes from the room
         map and is only as accurate as that map; a few tens of cm of error can leave
         it beside or behind the drone, out of frame, with nothing to servo onto.
         Standing off and looking is robust — a camera resolves a bearing far better
         than a map resolves a position. Clear BOTH ('') to switch staging off.

       goal_x/goal_y — THE PRE-SELECTION TARGET. Where A* flies the drone the moment
         the stack is up (a numeric goal => a route at once, flown on GO); it then
         HOLDS there, in the air, with nothing else happening — object_approach is
         disabled until a selection, so there is no aim, no sweep, no landing, no
         /cmd_vel hand-off. This is the "reach 0,-2 and wait" leg. EMPTY ('') instead
         idles the planners until a selection (no pre-planned route). Selecting an
         object always wins: the director republishes the goal at the room centre. -->
  <arg name="stage_x"         default="0.0" />   <!-- room centre: look for the object from here -->
  <arg name="stage_y"         default="-3.0" />
  <arg name="goal_x"          default="0.0" />   <!-- pre-selection target: fly here and hold -->
  <arg name="goal_y"          default="-2.0" />
  <!-- fallback by default, matching real_drone.launch: A* flies the route and NavDP
       rescues only a boxed-in A*. nav_mode:=hybrid hands NavDP the hard turns/doorways;
       astar is pure A*; combination is the always-on A*+NavDP fusion.
       hybrid / combination / fallback all need the NavDP server up. -->
  <arg name="nav_mode"        default="fallback" />
  <arg name="use_navdp"       default="false" />
  <!-- drift_pid controller (controller:=drift_pid) - generated block BEGIN -->
  <!-- SPEED AND FORCE  -  the per-axis envelope, and the multi-axis budget -->
  <arg name="dp_cruise_speed"            default="0.18" /><!-- m/s on a straight leg. THE main speed dial - raise this first -->
  <arg name="dp_cruise_straight" default="0.0" /><!-- m/s forward speed while the yaw correction is QUIET; blends down to dp_cruise_speed as yaw activity grows. 0 = off (single cruise everywhere) -->
  <arg name="dp_max_vx"                  default="0.25" /><!-- m/s hard cap FORWARD. 0.45 = full XTEND pitch thrust (600 counts) -->
  <arg name="dp_max_vx_back"             default="0.12" /><!-- m/s hard cap in REVERSE. Harder than forward: no rear camera, every backward metre is blind -->
  <arg name="dp_max_vy"                  default="0.12" /><!-- m/s hard cap sideways (ROLL). Weaker axis; keep well under max_vx -->
  <arg name="dp_max_wz"                  default="0.40" /><!-- rad/s hard cap yaw (615 of 1000 counts). 0.65 = full XTEND yaw thrust -->
  <arg name="dp_max_translation"         default="0.25" /><!-- m/s cap on the (vx,vy) vector, so a diagonal is not faster than an axis -->
  <arg name="dp_combined_effort"         default="1.4" /><!-- |vx|/max + |vy|/max + |wz|/max budget. 1.0 = one axis at full. -->
  <arg name="dp_accel_xy"                default="0.35" /><!-- m/s2 how fast translation may change. Low = gradual, keeps DA3 depth usable -->
  <arg name="dp_accel_wz"                default="1.2" /><!-- rad/s2 ramp-up rate of the yaw command -->
  <arg name="dp_decel_xy"                default="0.60" /><!-- m/s2 how fast translation may be taken OFF. >= accel: braking is never rate-limited by the gentle ramp-up -->
  <arg name="dp_decel_wz"                default="2.0" /><!-- rad/s2 how fast the yaw command may be taken off -->
  <arg name="dp_min_vx"                  default="0.06" /><!-- m/s smallest forward command the motors actually act on -->
  <arg name="dp_min_vy"                  default="0.06" /><!-- m/s smallest sideways command the motors actually act on -->
  <arg name="dp_min_wz_deg"              default="10.0" /><!-- deg/s smallest yaw command that actually rotates the drone (yaw bites late on this airframe) -->
  <arg name="dp_release_frac"            default="0.5" /><!-- below this fraction of a min the command is dropped to 0, above it snapped up -->
  <!-- NAVIGATION  -  how it gets to the next waypoint -->
  <arg name="dp_approach_yaw_rate"       default="0.35" /><!-- rad/s cap on the turn onto a leg -->
  <arg name="dp_track_yaw_rate" default="0.35" /><!-- rad/s yaw cap while TRACKING/station-keeping (turns onto a leg use dp_approach_yaw_rate); low = yaw only trims mid-leg and ROLL owns the line -->
  <arg name="dp_turn_pitch_bias"         default="0.08" /><!-- m/s FLOOR on forward speed while a TURN's yaw is active. Never backward while yawing: a backward pitch under a turn inverts the delivered yaw on this airframe (measured 2026-07-21); a small forward pitch makes the yaw bite (11% delivery in place vs 30-68% translating). 0 = no bite added, backward still forbidden -->
  <arg name="dp_turn_side_cone_deg"      default="35.0" /><!-- deg half-angle of the sideslip cone the translation may occupy while the yaw axis is active. YAW+ROLL is not the same manoeuvre as YAW+forward: |vy| is capped at tan(cone)*vx during an active yaw, so roll seasons the progress vector but never dominates it -->
  <arg name="dp_pos_radius"              default="0.30" /><!-- m waypoint capture radius -->
  <arg name="dp_slow_radius"             default="0.80" /><!-- m start slowing this far from the FINAL goal -->
  <arg name="dp_arrive_speed_min"        default="0.08" /><!-- m/s floor outside pos_radius, so it never crawls to a noisy stop -->
  <arg name="dp_lookahead_m"             default="0.60" /><!-- m how far ahead the heading aims. Bigger = smoother but cuts corners -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_engage_deg"          default="22.0" /><!-- deg heading error above which it turns; below it corrects with ROLL only -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_release_deg"         default="9.0" /><!-- deg error at which turning stops. MUST be < engage: the anti-chatter gap -->
  <arg name="dp_travel_cone_deg"         default="70.0" /><!-- deg widest angle off straight-ahead it will fly - never fast where the camera cannot see -->
  <arg name="dp_suppress_deg"            default="110.0" /><!-- deg error at which translation drops to suppress_floor (turn first, then fly) -->
  <arg name="dp_suppress_floor"          default="0.15" /><!-- fraction of speed kept beyond suppress_deg. >0 so it keeps creeping -->
  <arg name="dp_passed_bearing_deg"      default="110.0" /><!-- deg a non-final waypoint this far behind counts as passed, not turned back for -->
  <!-- TURN ANTICIPATION (yaw lookahead)  -  lead the nose into the next corner
       while the body keeps flying the leg on ROLL, so the drone arrives at the
       corner already pointing down the next one and flies straight out of it,
       instead of arriving pointed the old way and rotating in place (the
       manoeuvre this airframe is worst at: ~11% yaw delivery standing still,
       and standing still is where it drifts most). OFF by default - it changes
       how every corner is flown. See core/.../trackers/drift_pid/README.md. -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_lookahead"           default="false" /><!-- the master switch. true = anticipate corners, false = the classic stop-and-turn -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_lookahead_start_m"   default="2.5" /><!-- m before the corner the nose starts easing round. THE dial: bigger anticipates earlier and more gently but flies more of the leg crabbed (a crab is capped by the weak ROLL axis, so it is slower than a cruise); smaller demands a brisker rotation at the end. Scaled down for gentler corners -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_lookahead_align_m"   default="0.35" /><!-- m before the corner the nose is fully round; the last stretch is flown on pure roll. Keep at or just above dp_pos_radius, or the corner retires before it is reached -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_lookahead_corner_deg" default="25.0" /><!-- deg smallest route direction change that counts as a turn. Must sit clear of the ~10 deg weave a grid A* route leaves on a straight corridor -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_lookahead_confirm_m" default="1.0" /><!-- m of path past the corner used to read its outgoing heading. The run stops at the NEXT direction change, so turn-then-turn is anticipated one turn at a time -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_lookahead_max_deg"   default="70.0" /><!-- deg hard cap on how far the nose may lead the direction of travel. NOT a geometry limit: 90 would be exactly sideways, and a crab with no forward speed left is one this airframe can no longer yaw out of (~11% delivery standing still vs 30-68% translating). ~60 keeps half the progress vector forward, which is what holds the yaw authority; whatever is left of the turn is finished at the corner while moving onto the new leg -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_lookahead_catchup_deg" default="12.0" /><!-- deg the lead only advances while the heading error is inside this. Keeps the schedule from walking away from a drone that cannot follow it, and MUST stay below dp_yaw_engage_deg or the anticipation would trip the very stop-and-turn it exists to avoid -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_lookahead_rate"      default="0.25" /><!-- rad/s fastest the schedule may rotate the heading target, and the rate it budgets the approach against. MUST NOT exceed dp_track_yaw_rate (the manoeuvre runs in TRACK, so that is the whole budget it has); the node refuses to start otherwise, rather than fly a schedule that falls behind every corner. Kept a literal rather than an $(arg) reference so every layer of the launch chain declares the same default; the node falls back to dp_track_yaw_rate only when the param is not set at all -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_lookahead_cone_deg"  default="0.0" /><!-- deg sideslip cone while crabbing; 0 = none. Deliberately replaces dp_turn_side_cone_deg here, which caps |vy| at tan(cone)*vx and would cancel the manoeuvre outright at a full lead (vx = 0). Backward travel stays forbidden either way -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_lookahead_ff"        default="1.0" /><!-- 0..1 how much of the schedule's own rotation rate is fed straight to the yaw axis. 0 leaves the loop purely feedback, and the nose then sits a few degrees behind the plan -->
  <!-- STATION KEEPING  -  holding still, which is where fore/aft drift shows up -->
  <arg name="dp_alt_hold"                default="false" /><!-- altitude hold on the solved pose z: keep the drone at the tag-plane height (target follows cruise_z) -->
  <arg name="dp_alt_climb_max"           default="0.06" /><!-- m/s cap on UP; the guarded direction, keep tiny (vertical axis climbs far harder than nominal) -->
  <arg name="dp_alt_kp" default="0.5" /><!-- altitude-hold P gain, metres of height error -> m/s of climb/descent demand (tapered by this, capped by dp_alt_climb_max) -->
  <arg name="dp_alt_pulse_trigger_m" default="0.20" /><!-- m below target that starts a dedicated climb pulse (stop translating, climb, resume) -->
  <arg name="dp_alt_pulse_tscale" default="0.5" /><!-- (vx,vy) kept during a climb pulse. Below 1 so the climb wins the larger share of thrust, but high enough that forward flight CONTINUES through the climb (0.2 read as "no forward command" on the 2026-07-21 flight). 1.0 = climb and cruise at full speed simultaneously -->
  <arg name="dp_alt_ceiling_m"           default="1.2" /><!-- m; at/above this measured altitude a climb is NEVER commanded -->
  <arg name="dp_alt_conf_min"            default="0.35" /><!-- pose confidence required to climb; never climbs on a vague or coasted pose -->
  <arg name="dp_hold_deadband_m"         default="0.06" /><!-- m position error ignored while holding -->
  <arg name="dp_forward_track_frac"      default="0.0" /><!-- along-track PID during a straight leg. 0 = the cruise owns that axis -->
  <arg name="dp_lateral_turn_frac"       default="0.40" /><!-- fraction of the ROLL correction used while turning (a big roll spoils a turn) -->
  <arg name="dp_settle_map_updates"      default="0" /><!-- fresh voxel updates to wait for while stopped. 0 = do not force any -->
  <!-- DRIFT PID  -  the loops that LEARN the drift instead of just resisting it -->
  <arg name="dp_lat_kp"                  default="0.55" /><!-- cross-track P: metres of error -> m/s of ROLL -->
  <arg name="dp_lat_ki"                  default="0.06" /><!-- cross-track I: LEARNS the standing sideways drift. Raise to kill a constant offset -->
  <arg name="dp_lat_kd"                  default="0.12" /><!-- cross-track D: damping -->
  <arg name="dp_lat_i_limit"             default="0.05" /><!-- m/s biggest standing sideways push it may assume exists -->
  <arg name="dp_lat_max"                 default="0.10" /><!-- m/s cap on the whole cross-track correction. Must be <= dp_max_vy -->
  <arg name="dp_lat_deadband_m"          default="0.03" /><!-- m error ignored on a CRISP pose. THE TRACKING FLOOR; widens automatically as pos_std grows -->
  <arg name="dp_lat_d_tau_s"             default="0.4" /><!-- s low-pass on the derivative (a 10Hz noisy pose differentiates to noise) -->
  <arg name="dp_fwd_kp"                  default="0.50" /><!-- along-track P: metres -> m/s of PITCH, while turning or holding -->
  <arg name="dp_fwd_ki"                  default="0.05" /><!-- along-track I: LEARNS the standing fore/aft drift -->
  <arg name="dp_fwd_kd"                  default="0.10" /><!-- along-track D: damping -->
  <arg name="dp_fwd_i_limit"             default="0.05" /><!-- m/s biggest standing fore/aft push it may assume -->
  <arg name="dp_fwd_max"                 default="0.10" /><!-- m/s cap on the along-track correction -->
  <arg name="dp_fwd_deadband_m"          default="0.05" /><!-- m along-track error ignored on a crisp pose; widens with pos_std -->
  <arg name="dp_fwd_d_tau_s"             default="0.4" /><!-- s low-pass on the along-track derivative -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_kp"                  default="0.90" /><!-- heading P: rad of error -> rad/s of YAW -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_ki"                  default="0.08" /><!-- heading I: LEARNS the standing yaw drift (the rarest of the three) -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_kd"                  default="0.15" /><!-- heading D: damping -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_i_limit"             default="0.08" /><!-- rad/s biggest standing yaw push it may assume -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_max"                 default="0.35" /><!-- rad/s cap on the heading correction. Must be <= dp_max_wz -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_deadband_deg"        default="2.0" /><!-- deg heading error ignored -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_d_tau_s"             default="0.35" /><!-- s low-pass on the heading derivative -->
  <arg name="dp_drift_leak_s"            default="180.0" /><!-- s over which a learned drift fades. Long: it belongs to the airframe, not the minute -->
  <!-- LOCALIZATION TRUST  -  fly slower, and stop learning, when the pose is poor -->
  <arg name="dp_conf_full"               default="0.35" /><!-- confidence at/above which it flies full speed. NOT 0.9: a lone tag caps near 0.21 -->
  <arg name="dp_conf_min"                default="0.10" /><!-- confidence at/below which it flies at dp_speed_floor -->
  <arg name="dp_speed_floor"             default="0.35" /><!-- slowest speed multiplier on a poor pose. >0: creeping beats stopping in a corridor -->
  <arg name="dp_yaw_scale_floor"         default="0.0" /><!-- floor on the confidence speed scale as applied to YAW (1.0 = a vague pose never slows the turning, only the flying; turning is what sweeps tags back into view) -->
  <arg name="dp_gain_floor"              default="0.25" /><!-- smallest P/D scale on a poor pose. Lower than speed_floor: reacting to a vague pose is what injects noise -->
  <arg name="dp_conf_integrate"          default="0.18" /><!-- below this the drift loops FREEZE - never learn drift from a pose you do not trust -->
  <arg name="dp_conf_hold"               default="0.05" /><!-- below this the drone stops and holds -->
  <arg name="dp_max_age_s"               default="0.6" /><!-- s since the last pose before it stops. Silence is a signal on this stack -->
  <arg name="dp_coast_speed_scale"       default="0.5" /><!-- extra speed multiplier while dead-reckoning (no tag in view, ~0.5s budget) -->
  <arg name="dp_eff_floor"               default="0.15" /><!-- cmd_effectiveness at/below which the commands are not reaching the world -->
  <arg name="dp_eff_full"                default="0.60" /><!-- cmd_effectiveness at/above which commands count as fully effective -->
  <arg name="dp_eff_speed_floor"         default="0.5" /><!-- speed multiplier while commands are UNPROVEN (effectiveness starts at 0.3): first metres fly cautious, then speed is earned. 1.0 disables -->
  <arg name="dp_latency_s"               default="0.12" /><!-- s camera->control delay compensated by leading the pose along the last command; earned via effectiveness, 0 while coasting. 0 disables -->
  <arg name="dp_std_ref_m"               default="0.05" /><!-- m pos_std at/below which the pose counts as crisp (multi-tag fixes sit at 0.01-0.05) -->
  <arg name="dp_std_deadband_gain"       default="0.6" /><!-- extra tracking deadband per metre of pos_std above the crisp reference: never correct (or learn from) errors smaller than the pose's own stated accuracy -->
  <arg name="dp_deadband_extra_max_m"    default="0.15" /><!-- m cap on that widening, so a coasting pose (std up to 0.5) cannot switch corrections off entirely -->
  <arg name="dp_require_quality"         default="false" /><!-- true HOLDS the drone until the confidence topics arrive; false flies without them (and warns) -->
  <!-- STUCK DETECTION  -  noticing a wall the camera cannot see -->
  <arg name="dp_block_enabled"          default="true" /><!-- master switch: false = never detect a blockage, never escape, never report one -->
  <arg name="dp_block_window_s"          default="1.2" /><!-- s trailing window over which progress is measured -->
  <arg name="dp_block_min_vx"            default="0.07" /><!-- m/s below this the tick does not count as trying to move -->
  <arg name="dp_block_min_wz_deg"        default="12.0" /><!-- deg/s below this the tick does not count as trying to turn. Keep above dp_min_wz_deg -->
  <arg name="dp_block_min_dist_m"        default="0.06" /><!-- m commanded distance needed in the window before the ratio means anything -->
  <arg name="dp_block_min_yaw_deg"       default="7.0" /><!-- deg commanded rotation needed in the window -->
  <arg name="dp_block_progress_frac"     default="0.30" /><!-- achieved/commanded below this = not moving. Not 0: a heavy drone always under-delivers -->
  <arg name="dp_block_confirm_ticks"     default="5" /><!-- consecutive bad ticks before declaring a blockage (ticks, never a wall clock) -->
  <arg name="dp_block_clear_ticks"       default="3" /><!-- consecutive good ticks before clearing one -->
  <arg name="dp_block_use_effectiveness" default="true" /><!-- also believe the localization's own cmd_effectiveness verdict -->
  <!-- ESCAPE REFLEXES  -  what it does about it (planning owns the reroute) -->
  <arg name="dp_escape_brake_s"          default="0.4" /><!-- s stopped before doing anything - start the escape from rest, not from inertia -->
  <arg name="dp_escape_back_s"           default="0.7" /><!-- s reversing after a blocked forward, to break contact -->
  <arg name="dp_escape_back_speed"       default="0.10" /><!-- m/s of that reverse -->
  <arg name="dp_escape_probe_s"          default="0.8" /><!-- s rolling sideways to test whether that side is open -->
  <arg name="dp_escape_probe_speed"      default="0.10" /><!-- m/s of that sideways probe -->
  <arg name="dp_escape_settle_s"         default="0.5" /><!-- s held still afterwards, so the depth model gets a stationary frame -->
  <arg name="dp_escape_yaw_probe_s"      default="1.0" /><!-- s rolling clear of a wall that blocked a TURN (longer: escaping, not asking) -->
  <arg name="dp_escape_yaw_invert"       default="false" /><!-- flip which way it rolls to escape a blocked turn. THE one sign worth checking against reality -->
  <arg name="dp_escape_max_attempts"     default="2" /><!-- escapes per obstacle before it gives up and tells the planner (2 = one probe each way) -->
  <!-- BLOCKAGE MEMORY  -  the planner remembering what the controller found -->
  <arg name="use_blockage_memory"        default="true" /><!-- remember unseen obstacles and stop routing through them -->
  <arg name="blockage_radius_m"          default="0.35" /><!-- m marked impassable around a reported spot. >= the drone's half-width -->
  <arg name="blockage_ttl_s"             default="0.0" /><!-- s a blockage is remembered. 0 = forever, right for a static building -->
  <!-- drift_pid controller - generated block END -->
  <arg name="controller"      default="waypoint" /><!-- waypoint | multi_axis | pure_pursuit | roll_assist | drift_pid -->
  <!-- Follower-side pose denoising. false = fly the localization stream as
       published, so its own jitter and lag are visible rather than filtered. -->
  <arg name="cmd_vy_sign" default="1.0" /><!-- lateral (linear.y) sign at publish: -1 corrects the inversion measured on this airframe; must be exactly 1 or -1 -->
  <arg name="use_pose_estimator" default="true" />
  <!-- WAYPOINT-CONTROLLER SPEEDS (controller:=waypoint, this mission's default).
       The one-axis follower never translates and rotates at once, so these are
       independent: vel_x is every forward leg, yaw_rate every in-place turn.
       Ignored under pure_pursuit, which uses pp_cruise_speed / pp_max_yaw_rate. -->
  <arg name="vel_x"           default="0.25" /><!-- m/s forward -->
  <arg name="yaw_rate"        default="0.7" /><!-- rad/s in-place turn -->
  <!-- A pure-yaw twist leaves the platform flat, so the turn bites late and coasts.
       This much forward PITCH rides along with an otherwise pure-yaw twist; it is
       never added to a commanded forward leg. 0 = pure yaw (the old behaviour). -->
  <arg name="yaw_pitch_bias"  default="0.05" /><!-- m/s forward ridden on a turn in place -->
  <!-- How big one in-place yaw pulse may get, in control ticks. Graded pulses
       size a burst by DURATION: the tick count is snapped to an even number and
       clamped to [min_motion_ticks, this], so the grades are 2/4/6/... ticks and
       this sets the strongest one. At yaw_rate 0.7 and ctrl_rate_hz 10 a tick is
       ~4 deg, and the platform coasts a further ~15 deg after the command stops,
       so 8 ticks is ~32 deg commanded and ~47 deg of actual turn per burst.
       Raising it makes a big turn finish in fewer stop-and-measure cycles; the
       cost is more angle swept open-loop before the settle re-measures.
       NOTE yaw_burst_max_deg does NOT do this: it feeds the legacy swept-angle
       branch, which yaw_graded_pulses (on by default) bypasses entirely. -->
  <arg name="yaw_burst_grade_max_ticks" default="6" />
  <!-- Debug logging master switch; see nav_stack.launch. -->
  <arg name="debug"           default="false" />
  <arg name="thinking_log" default="false" />
  <arg name="thinking_log_path" default="$(optenv FALCON_THOUGHT_LOG)" />
  <arg name="thinking_window" default="false" />
  <!-- Certainty log (AprilTag/drift confidence vs. command); see nav_stack.launch. -->
  <arg name="certainty_log" default="true" />
  <arg name="certainty_log_path" default="$(optenv FALCON_CERTAINTY_LOG)" />
  <!-- Record BEV + routes + replan events for offline visual replay; see
       nav_stack.launch and tasks/planning/nav_debug/. -->
  <arg name="nav_debug_record" default="true" />
  <!-- Pure-pursuit speed + yaw force; see mission.yaml. Only used when
       controller:=pure_pursuit (pp_cruise_speed shadows ~vel_x there). -->
  <arg name="pp_max_yaw_rate"       default="0.45" />
  <arg name="pp_yaw_rate_smoothing" default="0.3" />
  <arg name="pp_cruise_speed"       default="0.2" />
  <arg name="pp_holonomic"          default="false" /><!-- false = no ROLL; yaw turns -->
  <arg name="cruise_z"        default="1.0" />       <!-- flight altitude; bev_z_peak follows it -->

  <!-- Camera intrinsics (raw K; shared by the map AND the detector). -->
  <arg name="cam_fx"          default="322.6351083474948" />
  <arg name="cam_fy"          default="323.3893307141174" />
  <arg name="cam_cx"          default="242.06479658679714" />
  <arg name="cam_cy"          default="90.03019076680604" />
  <arg name="cam_width"       default="504" />
  <arg name="cam_height"      default="294" />

  <!-- ── The GO gate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
       start_go:=false means the WHOLE pipeline runs (BEV, A*, detector, director,
       even object selection) but NOT ONE velocity command reaches the drone until
       GO. That is what lets you launch before/while taking off by hand without the
       stack fighting you. Press GO in the director window, or:
         rostopic pub -1 /mission/go std_msgs/Bool "data: true"
       Set start_go:=true to fly immediately, as before this gate existed. -->
  <arg name="start_go"        default="false" />
  <arg name="go_topic"        default="/mission/go" />
  <arg name="zero_on_close"   default="true" />  <!-- one zero twist on GO to false -->
  <arg name="cmd_vel_raw_topic" default="$(arg drone_ns)/cmd_vel_raw" />

  <!-- ── Lost-localization recovery ───────────────────────────────────
       The AprilTag pose only exists while a tag is in view; when it goes cold the
       drone would otherwise keep flying on its last cached pose. This stops it,
       then backs up / climbs / sweeps for a tag, and lands if nothing works.
       recovery_stale_s is the STOP (a couple of frames at ~7 Hz); recovery_ladder_s
       is when it starts manoeuvring, and the gap between them is what keeps a
       routine gap between markers from provoking a blind back-up. -->
  <arg name="recovery_enabled"       default="true" />
  <arg name="recovery_stale_s"       default="0.3" />
  <arg name="recovery_ladder_s"      default="1.0" />
  <!-- Before the stop, finish the move that was interrupted: mid-turn keep
       turning (the tag left the frame because we rotated it out), mid-advance
       give the metres back (we flew too close to it). Then hold still and look. -->
  <arg name="recovery_persist_enabled" default="true" />
  <arg name="recovery_persist_turn_s"  default="0.6" />
  <arg name="recovery_persist_back_s"  default="0.6" />
  <arg name="recovery_climb_enabled" default="true" />
  <arg name="recovery_climb_speed"      default="0.08" />
  <arg name="recovery_climb_duration_s" default="0.4" />
  <arg name="recovery_back_speed"      default="0.30" /><!-- ~0.45 m per rung, twice -->
  <arg name="recovery_back_duration_s" default="1.5" />
  <arg name="recovery_turn_dir"      default="right" />
  <arg name="recovery_turn_rate"     default="0.5" /><!-- rad/s; too slow = a sweep that never sweeps -->

  <!-- The object object_approach filters detections for BEFORE anything is
       selected. run_object_mission.sh sets this from the same config value it
       prompts the detector with (detector.init_target), because the two must
       agree: the detector publishes detections under its prompt's label, and
       object_approach ignores every label but this one. Left to disagree, the
       mission simply never confirms an object and never lands visually, with
       nothing louder than two heartbeats naming different things.
       The director overwrites both the moment an object is selected, so this only
       governs the window before that, which is also the whole of a run with no
       selection (or one whose director failed to start). -->
  <arg name="target_object"   default="refrigerator" />

  <!-- ── Mission director (object selection) ──────────────────────── -->
  <arg name="selection_mode"  default="gui" />          <!-- gui | random -->
  <arg name="objects_file"    default="" />             <!-- '' => node's package-relative objects.json -->
  <arg name="seed"            default="-1" />            <!-- >=0 => reproducible random pick -->

  <!-- ── Object-approach mission (visual servo + landing) ──────────── -->
  <arg name="lock_mode"       default="detector_tracker" />
  <arg name="closure_mode"    default="multi_axis" />
  <arg name="force_mode"      default="fixed" />
  <!-- Forward power of the closure (visual servo). In force_mode:=fixed the forward
       pulse magnitude IS fixed_vx; vx_max caps the servo's analog demand before the
       shaper snaps it to that pulse. Raise for more push toward the object (the
       airframe's forward ceiling is ~0.45 m/s). -->
  <arg name="vx_max"          default="0.4" />
  <arg name="fixed_vx"        default="0.4" />
  <!-- Acquisition radius: how close to the room-centre goal counts as "arrived" (the
       AIM trigger). Forgiving on purpose, as the room centre is a vantage point to look
       from, not a precise target to nail. -->
  <arg name="arrive_radius_m" default="0.8" />
  <!-- Forgiving radius on the pre-selection ENTRY point (goal_x/goal_y) that arms the
       visual take-over: no blind visual servo until the drone has flown into the room. -->
  <arg name="arm_point_radius_m" default="0.8" />
  <arg name="target_range_m"  default="0.5" />          <!-- visual hover standoff -->
  <!-- Visual-reach land distance (depth). land_range_m:=0 disables the visual land and
       relies on arrival-land alone. -->
  <arg name="land_range_m"       default="1.0" />
  <arg name="land_confirm_ticks" default="3" />
  <!-- Arrival-land (reached "by A* alone", from SEARCH): OFF for this mission.
       Arriving at the room centre must AIM then SWEEP, never land on arrival. The
       give-up land is scan_land_revolutions (below); a real object reach still lands
       via land_range_m. -->
  <arg name="land_at_goal"              default="false" />
  <arg name="arrive_land_confirm_ticks" default="5" />
  <arg name="min_score"       default="0.15" />
  <arg name="n_confirm"       default="3" />

  <!-- ── The AIM: what the drone does on reaching the staging point ────
       Turn the nose onto the object's bearing in pulsed bursts (the platform's yaw
       is discrete and coasts, so a burst is aimed aim_yaw_coast_deg short and the
       coast lands it), then HOLD STILL for aim_look_s so the detector gets clean,
       blur-free frames down that bearing. Confirming there is the good outcome:
       the visual servo takes over and closes on the object it can actually see.
       Failing that, the goal is re-published at the object's own (x,y) and the
       mission continues exactly as it did before staging existed. -->
  <arg name="aim_before_direct" default="true" />   <!-- false => no aim; fly the goal straight through -->
  <arg name="aim_tolerance_deg" default="12.0" />   <!-- "pointing at it"; camera HFOV is ~76 deg -->
  <arg name="aim_look_s"        default="4.0" />    <!-- look this long before giving up on seeing it -->
  <arg name="aim_settle_s"      default="1.0" />    <!-- stop between bursts so the coast finishes -->
  <arg name="aim_timeout_s"     default="25.0" />   <!-- cap: a drone that will not turn still escalates/sweeps -->
  <!-- A failed aim SWEEPS the room in place for the object (true) rather than flying
       onto its imprecise catalogued coordinate (false). ON for this mission: the
       small-room position is not trusted enough to fly onto. -->
  <arg name="aim_fail_to_scan"  default="true" />
  <!-- Give-up land: after this many full in-place turns of the sweep with no
       detection, land where we are. 0 = sweep forever. -->
  <arg name="scan_land_revolutions" default="3" />
  <arg name="object_position_topic" default="/object_approach/object_position" />

  <!-- ── Viewers (need a display) ─────────────────────────────────── -->
  <arg name="viewer"          default="true" />         <!-- live target-lock HUD window -->
  <arg name="bev_viewer"      default="true" />         <!-- interactive BEV window (from real_drone.launch) -->
  <arg name="publish_overlay" default="true" />

  <!-- ══ Nav stack: flies to goal_x/goal_y (empty => idle until selection). ══ -->
  <!-- ══ A* planner (route search + replanning) ══
       Defaults mirror the layer below; see nav_stack.launch for the full
       per-parameter notes. Set these from config/mission.yaml. -->
  <arg name="waypoint_spacing_m"            default="1.5" />

  <!-- How wide "in front of the next point" is; see mission.yaml. -->
  <arg name="yaw_acquisition_radius"        default="0.2" />
  <arg name="yaw_acquire_max_deg"           default="35.0" />
  <arg name="skip_yaw_thresh"               default="0.25" /><!-- rad; 14.3 deg -->
  <!-- 40 cm hard wall standoff on the CRUISE legs, matching the nav stack. If a
       target object sits closer than this to a wall its goal cell is lethal and
       gets snapped out by goal_snap_radius_m; lower this (or hand the terminal
       leg to object_approach) when you must close on a wall-adjacent object. -->
  <arg name="inflate_radius_m"              default="0.40" />
  <arg name="unknown_blocked"               default="false" />
  <arg name="unknown_cost"                  default="6.0" />
  <!-- Soft wall avoidance + confidence-weighted lethality; see nav_stack.launch. -->
  <arg name="clearance_weight"              default="3.0" />
  <arg name="clearance_margin_m"            default="0.8" />
  <arg name="lethal_confidence"             default="0.5" />
  <arg name="soft_obstacle_cost"            default="25.0" />
  <!-- Relaxable standoff; see nav_stack.launch. -->
  <arg name="inflate_floor_m"               default="0.25" />
  <arg name="relax_step_m"                  default="0.05" />
  <arg name="probe_radius_m"                default="0.10" />
  <arg name="replan_relaxed_period_s"       default="4.0" />
  <arg name="los_smoothing"                 default="false" />
  <arg name="turn_penalty"                  default="0.3" />
  <arg name="heading_penalty_m"             default="1.5" />
  <arg name="connectivity"                  default="4" />
  <arg name="search_margin_m"               default="3.0" />
  <arg name="start_skip_m"                  default="0.5" />
  <arg name="goal_snap_radius_m"            default="2.0" />
  <arg name="min_free_cells_to_plan"        default="80" />
  <arg name="smart_replan"                  default="true" />
  <arg name="replan_corridor_radius_m"      default="1.0" />
  <arg name="replan_min_new_cells"          default="60" />
  <arg name="replan_min_new_cells_any"      default="240" />
  <arg name="replan_rotation_min_deg"       default="30.0" />
  <!-- Periodic tick adopts with no length test; see nav_stack.launch. -->
  <arg name="replan_periodic_always"        default="false" />
  <arg name="replan_period_s"               default="7.0" />
  <arg name="replan_commit_min_s"           default="4.0" />
  <arg name="replan_improve_frac"           default="0.15" />
  <arg name="stop_on_blocked_plan_fail"     default="true" />
  <arg name="replan_collision_confirm"      default="2" />
  <arg name="plan_period_s"                 default="10.0" />
  <arg name="replan_on_collision"           default="false" />
  <arg name="replan_on_bev"                 default="false" />
  <arg name="corner_round"                  default="false" />
  <arg name="corner_merge_deg"              default="8.0" />
  <arg name="corner_max_turn_deg"           default="14.0" />
  <arg name="corner_chamfer_max_deg"        default="28.0" />
  <arg name="corner_chamfer_dist_m"         default="0.5" />
  <arg name="corner_min_runup_m"            default="0.6" />
  <arg name="replan_on_predicted_collision" default="false" />
  <arg name="max_predicted_replans"         default="3" />

  <!-- ══ BEV map (occupancy the planner searches) ══
       Defaults mirror the layer below; see nav_stack.launch for the full
       per-parameter notes. Set these from config/mission.yaml. -->
  <arg name="bev_resolution"             default="0.10" />
  <arg name="bev_xmin"                   default="-6.0" />
  <arg name="bev_ymin"                   default="-6.0" />
  <arg name="bev_xmax"                   default="6.0" />
  <arg name="bev_ymax"                   default="6.0" />
  <arg name="bev_bbox_margin"            default="1.0" />
  <arg name="bev_publish_hz"             default="10.0" />
  <arg name="bev_occ_dilate"             default="0" />
  <arg name="bev_z_floor"                default="0.70" />
  <arg name="bev_z_ceil"                 default="1.50" />
  <arg name="bev_z_peak"                 default="$(arg cruise_z)" />
  <arg name="bev_weight_profile"         default="triangular" />
  <arg name="bev_weight_sigma"           default="0.50" />
  <arg name="bev_voxel_size"             default="$(arg bev_resolution)" />
  <arg name="bev_occ_weight_thresh"      default="2.0" />
  <arg name="bev_min_occ_voxels"         default="4" />
  <arg name="bev_min_free_voxels"        default="1" />
  <arg name="bev_confirm_3d"             default="true" />
  <arg name="bev_neighbors_3d"           default="6" />
  <arg name="bev_min_occ_neighbors_3d"   default="1" />
  <arg name="bev_min_wall_run"           default="3" />
  <arg name="bev_min_component_cells"    default="0" />
  <arg name="bev_component_connectivity" default="8" />
  <arg name="bev_protect_openings"       default="true" />
  <arg name="bev_door_band_m"            default="0.80" />
  <arg name="bev_door_free_voxels"       default="2" />
  <arg name="bev_door_occ_tol"           default="0" />
  <arg name="bev_wall_fill_mode"         default="directional" />
  <arg name="bev_wall_fill_neighbors"    default="5" />
  <arg name="bev_wall_fill_iters"        default="1" />
  <arg name="bev_temporal_filter"        default="true" />
  <arg name="bev_occ_conf_full"          default="3.0" />
  <arg name="bev_t_inc"                  default="1.0" />
  <arg name="bev_t_dec"                  default="1.0" />
  <arg name="bev_t_max"                  default="5.0" />
  <arg name="bev_t_on"                   default="2.0" />
  <arg name="bev_t_off"                  default="0.5" />
  <arg name="bev_always_recompute"       default="false" />
  <arg name="bev_skip_unchanged_publish" default="true" />

  <!-- ══ Path corrector / ESDF / simplifier ══
       Defaults mirror the layer below; see nav_stack.launch for the full
       per-parameter notes. Set these from config/mission.yaml. -->
  <arg name="corrector"                    default="potential_field" />
  <arg name="esdf_target_clearance_m"      default="0.2" />
  <arg name="esdf_max_total_shift_m"       default="0.5" />
  <arg name="esdf_max_step_m"              default="0.2" />
  <arg name="esdf_iterations"              default="12" />
  <arg name="esdf_lateral_only"            default="true" />
  <arg name="esdf_smooth_sigma_m"          default="0.1" />
  <arg name="esdf_occ_thresh"              default="0.65" />
  <arg name="resample_min_spacing_m"       default="0.3" />
  <arg name="simplify_debug"               default="$(arg debug)" />
  <arg name="simplify_merge"               default="true" />
  <arg name="simplify_merge_radius_m"      default="0.20" />
  <arg name="simplify_zigzag"              default="true" />
  <arg name="simplify_zigzag_angle_deg"    default="60.0" />
  <arg name="simplify_zigzag_strength"     default="0.5" />
  <arg name="simplify_zigzag_passes"       default="1" />
  <arg name="simplify_collinear"           default="true" />
  <arg name="simplify_collinear_angle_deg" default="10.0" />
  <arg name="simplify_max_segment_m"       default="3.0" />
  <arg name="simplify_min_spacing"         default="true" />
  <arg name="simplify_min_spacing_m"       default="1.0" />
  <arg name="simplify_turn_keep_deg"       default="25.0" />

  <!-- ══ APF / safety correction ══
       Defaults mirror the layer below; see nav_stack.launch for the full
       per-parameter notes. Set these from config/mission.yaml. -->
  <arg name="safety_correct"            default="true" />
  <arg name="apf_centering"             default="line_search" />
  <arg name="apf_gain"                  default="0.5" />
  <arg name="apf_max_total_shift_m"     default="0.5" />
  <arg name="apf_min_clearance_m"       default="0.2" />
  <arg name="apf_debug"                 default="$(arg debug)" />
  <arg name="apf_collision_recheck"     default="true" />
  <arg name="apf_treat_unknown_as_free" default="true" />
  <arg name="apf_unknown_damping"       default="true" />
  <arg name="apf_unknown_radius_m"      default="0.5" />
  <arg name="publish_forces"            default="true" />
  <arg name="force_arrow_scale"         default="0.5" />
  <arg name="publish_force_field"       default="true" />
  <arg name="force_field_stride"        default="4" />

  <include file="$(find falcon_adapter)/launch/real_drone.launch">
    <!-- GO gate: hold every command until GO (see start_go above). -->
    <arg name="start_go"          value="$(arg start_go)" />
    <arg name="go_topic"          value="$(arg go_topic)" />
    <arg name="zero_on_close"     value="$(arg zero_on_close)" />
    <!-- Lost-localization recovery (see above). -->
    <arg name="recovery_enabled"       value="$(arg recovery_enabled)" />
    <arg name="recovery_stale_s"       value="$(arg recovery_stale_s)" />
    <arg name="recovery_ladder_s"      value="$(arg recovery_ladder_s)" />
    <arg name="recovery_persist_enabled" value="$(arg recovery_persist_enabled)" />
    <arg name="recovery_persist_turn_s"  value="$(arg recovery_persist_turn_s)" />
    <arg name="recovery_persist_back_s"  value="$(arg recovery_persist_back_s)" />
    <arg name="recovery_climb_enabled" value="$(arg recovery_climb_enabled)" />
    <arg name="recovery_climb_speed"      value="$(arg recovery_climb_speed)" />
    <arg name="recovery_climb_duration_s" value="$(arg recovery_climb_duration_s)" />
    <arg name="recovery_back_speed"      value="$(arg recovery_back_speed)" />
    <arg name="recovery_back_duration_s" value="$(arg recovery_back_duration_s)" />
    <arg name="recovery_turn_dir"      value="$(arg recovery_turn_dir)" />
    <arg name="recovery_turn_rate"     value="$(arg recovery_turn_rate)" />
    <arg name="cmd_vel_raw_topic" value="$(arg cmd_vel_raw_topic)" />
    <arg name="cruise_z"        value="$(arg cruise_z)" />
    <!-- A* planner (route search + replanning) -->
    <arg name="waypoint_spacing_m"            value="$(arg waypoint_spacing_m)" />
    <arg name="yaw_acquisition_radius"        value="$(arg yaw_acquisition_radius)" />
    <arg name="yaw_acquire_max_deg"           value="$(arg yaw_acquire_max_deg)" />
    <arg name="skip_yaw_thresh"               value="$(arg skip_yaw_thresh)" />
    <arg name="inflate_radius_m"              value="$(arg inflate_radius_m)" />
    <arg name="unknown_blocked"               value="$(arg unknown_blocked)" />
    <arg name="unknown_cost"                  value="$(arg unknown_cost)" />
    <arg name="clearance_weight"              value="$(arg clearance_weight)" />
    <arg name="clearance_margin_m"            value="$(arg clearance_margin_m)" />
    <arg name="lethal_confidence"             value="$(arg lethal_confidence)" />
    <arg name="soft_obstacle_cost"            value="$(arg soft_obstacle_cost)" />
    <arg name="inflate_floor_m"               value="$(arg inflate_floor_m)" />
    <arg name="relax_step_m"                  value="$(arg relax_step_m)" />
    <arg name="probe_radius_m"                value="$(arg probe_radius_m)" />
    <arg name="replan_relaxed_period_s"       value="$(arg replan_relaxed_period_s)" />
    <arg name="los_smoothing"                 value="$(arg los_smoothing)" />
    <arg name="turn_penalty"                  value="$(arg turn_penalty)" />
    <arg name="heading_penalty_m"             value="$(arg heading_penalty_m)" />
    <arg name="connectivity"                  value="$(arg connectivity)" />
    <arg name="search_margin_m"               value="$(arg search_margin_m)" />
    <arg name="start_skip_m"                  value="$(arg start_skip_m)" />
    <arg name="goal_snap_radius_m"            value="$(arg goal_snap_radius_m)" />
    <arg name="min_free_cells_to_plan"        value="$(arg min_free_cells_to_plan)" />
    <arg name="smart_replan"                  value="$(arg smart_replan)" />
    <arg name="replan_corridor_radius_m"      value="$(arg replan_corridor_radius_m)" />
    <arg name="replan_min_new_cells"          value="$(arg replan_min_new_cells)" />
    <arg name="replan_min_new_cells_any"      value="$(arg replan_min_new_cells_any)" />
    <arg name="replan_rotation_min_deg"       value="$(arg replan_rotation_min_deg)" />
    <arg name="replan_periodic_always"        value="$(arg replan_periodic_always)" />
    <arg name="replan_period_s"               value="$(arg replan_period_s)" />
    <arg name="replan_commit_min_s"           value="$(arg replan_commit_min_s)" />
    <arg name="replan_improve_frac"           value="$(arg replan_improve_frac)" />
    <arg name="stop_on_blocked_plan_fail"     value="$(arg stop_on_blocked_plan_fail)" />
    <arg name="replan_collision_confirm"      value="$(arg replan_collision_confirm)" />
    <arg name="plan_period_s"                 value="$(arg plan_period_s)" />
    <arg name="replan_on_collision"           value="$(arg replan_on_collision)" />
    <arg name="replan_on_bev"                 value="$(arg replan_on_bev)" />
    <arg name="corner_round"                  value="$(arg corner_round)" />
    <arg name="corner_merge_deg"              value="$(arg corner_merge_deg)" />
    <arg name="corner_max_turn_deg"           value="$(arg corner_max_turn_deg)" />
    <arg name="corner_chamfer_max_deg"        value="$(arg corner_chamfer_max_deg)" />
    <arg name="corner_chamfer_dist_m"         value="$(arg corner_chamfer_dist_m)" />
    <arg name="corner_min_runup_m"            value="$(arg corner_min_runup_m)" />
    <arg name="replan_on_predicted_collision" value="$(arg replan_on_predicted_collision)" />
    <arg name="max_predicted_replans"         value="$(arg max_predicted_replans)" />
    <!-- BEV map (occupancy the planner searches) -->
    <arg name="bev_resolution"             value="$(arg bev_resolution)" />
    <arg name="bev_xmin"                   value="$(arg bev_xmin)" />
    <arg name="bev_ymin"                   value="$(arg bev_ymin)" />
    <arg name="bev_xmax"                   value="$(arg bev_xmax)" />
    <arg name="bev_ymax"                   value="$(arg bev_ymax)" />
    <arg name="bev_bbox_margin"            value="$(arg bev_bbox_margin)" />
    <arg name="bev_publish_hz"             value="$(arg bev_publish_hz)" />
    <arg name="bev_occ_dilate"             value="$(arg bev_occ_dilate)" />
    <arg name="bev_z_floor"                value="$(arg bev_z_floor)" />
    <arg name="bev_z_ceil"                 value="$(arg bev_z_ceil)" />
    <arg name="bev_z_peak"                 value="$(arg bev_z_peak)" />
    <arg name="bev_weight_profile"         value="$(arg bev_weight_profile)" />
    <arg name="bev_weight_sigma"           value="$(arg bev_weight_sigma)" />
    <arg name="bev_voxel_size"             value="$(arg bev_voxel_size)" />
    <arg name="bev_occ_weight_thresh"      value="$(arg bev_occ_weight_thresh)" />
    <arg name="bev_min_occ_voxels"         value="$(arg bev_min_occ_voxels)" />
    <arg name="bev_min_free_voxels"        value="$(arg bev_min_free_voxels)" />
    <arg name="bev_confirm_3d"             value="$(arg bev_confirm_3d)" />
    <arg name="bev_neighbors_3d"           value="$(arg bev_neighbors_3d)" />
    <arg name="bev_min_occ_neighbors_3d"   value="$(arg bev_min_occ_neighbors_3d)" />
    <arg name="bev_min_wall_run"           value="$(arg bev_min_wall_run)" />
    <arg name="bev_min_component_cells"    value="$(arg bev_min_component_cells)" />
    <arg name="bev_component_connectivity" value="$(arg bev_component_connectivity)" />
    <arg name="bev_protect_openings"       value="$(arg bev_protect_openings)" />
    <arg name="bev_door_band_m"            value="$(arg bev_door_band_m)" />
    <arg name="bev_door_free_voxels"       value="$(arg bev_door_free_voxels)" />
    <arg name="bev_door_occ_tol"           value="$(arg bev_door_occ_tol)" />
    <arg name="bev_wall_fill_mode"         value="$(arg bev_wall_fill_mode)" />
    <arg name="bev_wall_fill_neighbors"    value="$(arg bev_wall_fill_neighbors)" />
    <arg name="bev_wall_fill_iters"        value="$(arg bev_wall_fill_iters)" />
    <arg name="bev_temporal_filter"        value="$(arg bev_temporal_filter)" />
    <arg name="bev_occ_conf_full"          value="$(arg bev_occ_conf_full)" />
    <arg name="bev_t_inc"                  value="$(arg bev_t_inc)" />
    <arg name="bev_t_dec"                  value="$(arg bev_t_dec)" />
    <arg name="bev_t_max"                  value="$(arg bev_t_max)" />
    <arg name="bev_t_on"                   value="$(arg bev_t_on)" />
    <arg name="bev_t_off"                  value="$(arg bev_t_off)" />
    <arg name="bev_always_recompute"       value="$(arg bev_always_recompute)" />
    <arg name="bev_skip_unchanged_publish" value="$(arg bev_skip_unchanged_publish)" />
    <!-- Path corrector / ESDF / simplifier -->
    <arg name="corrector"                    value="$(arg corrector)" />
    <arg name="esdf_target_clearance_m"      value="$(arg esdf_target_clearance_m)" />
    <arg name="esdf_max_total_shift_m"       value="$(arg esdf_max_total_shift_m)" />
    <arg name="esdf_max_step_m"              value="$(arg esdf_max_step_m)" />
